Patchsu patch 10 (optional): perfect-play PP in song select (forked from Ritsu).

Needs only 0001 (applies to plain osu!lazer 8cb6e6e68d + 0001). Also applies together with 0002–0008.

Ported from Ritsu's "sort and group beatmaps by perfect-play PP" (Ritsu contributors, MIT), with its later fixes.

  Sort:   "PP (perfect play)"  highest PP of an SS first.
          "Farmability"        1000 × PP ÷ seconds ÷ stars² (length and stars with the selected mods).
  Group:  "PP perfect play"    groups of "PP step" width (0 - 100 pp, 100 - 200 pp, ...), then "Calculating PP...", "No PP".
  Row:    right-click "Show converts" (tooltip "Right clickable") to show / hide the PP row:
          "PP max" range (0 – 1000, top = "1,000+" = no limit; only applies while the row is shown), coloured like
          the star rating bar. Settings → Patchsu → "Patch 10. PP aware beatmap carousel" → "Remove the 1,000 pp cap of the PP slider"
          makes it 0 – 3000 (top = ∞); with the cap on, PP groups above 1,000 become one "1,000+ pp" group
          (PP values themselves are never capped). With 0005, right / middle-click work on it like on the star bar.
          "PP step" (10 – 1000, saved), "PP calc" (off = only use already calculated values, saved). "PP calc" is as wide
          as "Show converts" and sits right under it on the same slanted lines; the "PP max" range takes the rest. Held
          down, it shrinks like "Show converts" and the "PP max" range follows.

- Values follow the selected ruleset and every selected mod (HD, NF etc. too), and re-sort when mods or their
  settings change. Missing values are calculated one by one in the background; the search bar shows
  "Calculating PP: x / y" and the list refreshes every second. Calculation pauses while song select isn't the
  current screen. Beatmaps still being calculated sort last and aren't hidden by the PP range yet.
- Values are cached in <data>/osu-local/perfect-pp-cache.json (key: ruleset, difficulty calculator version,
  beatmap hash, mods).
- Not ported: Ritsu's "PP earned" grouping (needs Ritsu's profiles) and its middle-click reverse sort (0005 has
  right-click reverse, which also works for the new sorts).

How it works (for later patches):
- New files: Screens/Select/PerfectPerformanceCache.cs, PerfectPerformanceSession.cs,
  BeatmapCarousel.PerfectPerformance.cs, FilterControl.PerformanceOptions.cs, PerfectPerformanceSettings.cs
  (the Settings → Patchsu subsection; the tab comes from 0001).
- Small hunks in FilterControl.cs, FilterCriteria.cs, BeatmapCarousel.cs, BeatmapCarouselFilter{Matching,Sorting,
  Grouping}.cs, SongSelect.cs, Sort/GroupMode.cs and OsuConfigManager.cs, placed away from 0002/0005's hunks.
  The PP sorts are cases in the sorter's compare(), so 0005's reverse flag applies to them.

